{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1567531833,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU0ODg3MzIxOTU=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3649","origin":"github"},"title":"Add feedback submission to cmdline crash handler","message":"Both @yarikoptic and I had the impression that we do not get enough feedback on cases where datalad doesn't work as intended and crashes. One possibility to mitigate this situation would be to add an automated feedback submission ability to the cmdline interface's crash handler. It could format a document with:\n\n- sys.argv\n- traceback of the crash\n- wtf output\n\nGiven that such a report could contain sensitive information, we should allow users to scan/edit such a report before it is sent (unless configured to be OK).\n\nMaybe there is already some tool that would facilitate the server-side of things.","files":null}]}